{"title":"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Synthetic_Geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Synthetic Geometry)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Part_1:_If_,_then\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Part 1: If , then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d1dd07d1baac8bfead12395e9b79b9726f4084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ \\perp EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /></span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Part_2:_If_,_then\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Part 2: If , then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39c134d9eeaf3bf929d13b7bdd2545673458401e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QE = QF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /></span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Conclusion\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Conclusion</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an isosceles triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ac37c9fa391eebb9601bfaca8bfbfaabdf5ca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the point on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0964c9cf406ef8e5ec8beaa6a92125f2d8f90460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is an arbitrary point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> different from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/0/200cef6bdf34aa21da8bdcbf721a3c6cb9feb45f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E, Q, F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> are distinct and collinear. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e523074f8e48f3c3e9e81ea84cfb36ddaa7b28a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39c134d9eeaf3bf929d13b7bdd2545673458401e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QE = QF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411ef29ce6c32ab71534dfd3319a6fe72af9c5ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d794967bd855edced950369620307257fee99f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> respectively such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/b/e4bc1a93fedca14b2b952927f7c2ae6948891276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E&#39;F&#39;\\perp OQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" />. Then, by the first part of the problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28c4f44a2aaac6bfac116287dd52def0d9688116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QE&#39;=QF&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/c/5cc137545461880d37a42ed28a121a469800a4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E&#39;F&#39;$\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" />, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b25bb6d3484dd48bb6f8f1d700381e4a3444c991.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EE&#39;FF&#39;$\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> is a parallelogram. Unless <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/3/b33d60140114038e1f5bac0ba7055cb0cf014d85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E=E&#39;$\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/6/c46b752475807cdae24338b432148b218feba45b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F=F&#39;$\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />, this is a contradiction since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8ff6a275e4e17362e234e7cfb54d2064159f8b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EE&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/0/c502c32405982bbd8ffa63042cc181cb3b09fea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F&#39;F$\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/3/b33d60140114038e1f5bac0ba7055cb0cf014d85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E=E&#39;$\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/6/c46b752475807cdae24338b432148b218feba45b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F=F&#39;$\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/d/1bd2258be663d5ccb0a96e55683493159b7be3a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ\\perp EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />, as desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Synthetic_Geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Synthetic_Geometry)\">Solution 2 (Synthetic Geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Synthetic Geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:IMO1994_Problem2.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a0/IMO1994_Problem2.jpg/750px-IMO1994_Problem2.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"750\" height=\"417\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a0/IMO1994_Problem2.jpg/1125px-IMO1994_Problem2.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/a0/IMO1994_Problem2.jpg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><br />\nWithout loss of generality, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> lie on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/5/4d5ee546f7ea84755eae7a58fbf1d892bd258118.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/6/ff687101ea39bca2d6db8f21b5ec0f5777906d9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = \\angle ACB = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"170\" height=\"14\" />, and define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f614ef66cb0e1ee92016517f545d3fb6f440f97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta = 90^\\circ - \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ac37c9fa391eebb9601bfaca8bfbfaabdf5ca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> is the axis of symmetry of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />, which by symmetry implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4bc4aa3bf95444cc15ace568757a441f807cebb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC \\perp AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbe3dad573a40e40df75f4fc3d2527fd099262dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OBC = \\angle OCB = 90^\\circ - \\theta = \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"255\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Part_1:_If_.2C_then\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Part_1:_If_,_then\">Part 1: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39c134d9eeaf3bf929d13b7bdd2545673458401e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QE = QF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d1dd07d1baac8bfead12395e9b79b9726f4084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ \\perp EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Part 1: If , then\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39c134d9eeaf3bf929d13b7bdd2545673458401e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QE = QF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<ol><li><b>Auxiliary Construction:</b> Construct a line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, intersecting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf34600128970159c6aea49612f455fd8e825a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> is also isosceles with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/0/a20edeb288d3ee8875d6fae17bba302a0391728b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = AW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/a/88af2bbb7e5c80e5ad423d2f80077b2585bf7fed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AEW = \\angle AWE = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"181\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f1902b98afdd1dcc678c234713cb4318fd69e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> is bisected by the axis of symmetry <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f1902b98afdd1dcc678c234713cb4318fd69e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li><b>Midline Properties:</b> In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/1/471394c95d55598560a95a3ecdb59d4bf1567840.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EFW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f1902b98afdd1dcc678c234713cb4318fd69e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/6591971ce08a5b9c6ff038ad43445bf9d95d5954.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$VQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> is a midline of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/1/471394c95d55598560a95a3ecdb59d4bf1567840.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EFW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1fcaae74fb69e945abbd9568cd80969eef68b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$VQ \\parallel FW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" /> (which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/c/afcca1e9405ebce2195302746b33e64b80684ec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$VQ \\parallel AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />), yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/6/cf6296cadf3b7826c44a9849433637e1b5b1deb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle VQB = \\angle ACB = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" />.</li>\n<li><b>Cyclic Quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/4/cd4321b3aa959c0da978c2887f3774957891621e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BVQO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />:</b> In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/f/cbfd0ad557c8b9d1f75e30bf0d6782d2202ff4eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABM$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b518514a5f8fe9982f48a13e49fabaa49e40090.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM \\perp BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/f/e9f37a32197735f1bb02828eef25e9c81ab566dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB \\perp AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddf1ee7a4d1e7f256ebde7da1a4c6ecd7460ba75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle VOB = \\angle AOB = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"171\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/c/afc80dfe541568ce97a2ea64cf174fbe135b86fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle VQB = \\theta = \\angle VOB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" />, the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2eeccf3864bb98a44df95b1064117b7d40e9097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B, V, Q, O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" /> are concyclic (i.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/4/cd4321b3aa959c0da978c2887f3774957891621e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BVQO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral).</li>\n<li><b>Congruence and Cyclic Quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/5898b16b4e04e69e17d551fe1d07553f814c31c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEQO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />:</b> By symmetry of the parallel construction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81acca1f5bef33bcef03e86c947cad94e07177b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EBQ \\cong \\triangle VBQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/101800ca4ecfda990c6b6782c68290b0f8ae7ec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEQ = \\angle BVQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/4/cd4321b3aa959c0da978c2887f3774957891621e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BVQO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral, the opposite angles satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/0/aa007275635d74c515837c0da9d5fcd09ec69f6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BVQ + \\angle BOQ = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" />. Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/2/4b252bcb9c97c525e0a7c7e70c2bcabef9397022.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BVQ = \\angle BEQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />, we get:</li></ol>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/e/3eed4e8202ff5a6f24b68985065923b79db64830.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BEQ + \\angle BOQ = 180^\\circ\\]\" width=\"191\" height=\"16\" />\nThis establishes that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/5898b16b4e04e69e17d551fe1d07553f814c31c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEQO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> is also a cyclic quadrilateral.\n</p>\n<ol><li><b>Perpendicularity Verification:</b> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/5898b16b4e04e69e17d551fe1d07553f814c31c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEQO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> is cyclic, the sum of its opposite angles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c4460b5100c3ce982ab5ebb20a8c3871e9cfdc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />:</li></ol>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/2/5d2bda9a8158a327d05e3a5755b892b8a90f6e4c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle EBO + \\angle EQO = 180^\\circ\\]\" width=\"191\" height=\"16\" />\nGiven that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/f/e9f37a32197735f1bb02828eef25e9c81ab566dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB \\perp AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4fedd112d90495505fa97422f042e7f4355c4ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EBO = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8a3c15c5e028f7e92365f2fb0df7290e5940ffd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle EQO = 180^\\circ - 90^\\circ = 90^\\circ\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"16\" />\nThis proves that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d1dd07d1baac8bfead12395e9b79b9726f4084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ \\perp EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Part_2:_If_.2C_then\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Part_2:_If_,_then\">Part 2: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d1dd07d1baac8bfead12395e9b79b9726f4084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ \\perp EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39c134d9eeaf3bf929d13b7bdd2545673458401e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QE = QF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Part 2: If , then\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d1dd07d1baac8bfead12395e9b79b9726f4084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ \\perp EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<ol><li><b>Cyclic Quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43f28d9899f60bd3f4b896d61366513c7ff35ab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QOFC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />:</b> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/e/67e413b11183c4569b89b22a8224498b099f600e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EBO + \\angle EQO = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/271ba7c0658cc829842ca96978a844527605b731.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EQOB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral. By angle chasing:</li></ol>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/5/b7520fcbf7c75b25fc895295c9cc4d02e6d276a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle QOC = \\angle QFC = \\beta \\quad (\\text{subtending base } QC)\\]\" width=\"350\" height=\"18\" />\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43f28d9899f60bd3f4b896d61366513c7ff35ab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QOFC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral.\n</p>\n<ol><li><b>Isosceles Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/899899a2f10f1ac00c700d284d6530bd71dbac89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EOF$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />:</b> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43f28d9899f60bd3f4b896d61366513c7ff35ab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QOFC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> is cyclic, the angles subtending the common base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e523074f8e48f3c3e9e81ea84cfb36ddaa7b28a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> are equal:</li></ol>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/6/cf66ac82181b25f0c1c2f7052bafcf2e45dded4a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle OCQ = \\angle OFQ \\quad (\\text{subtending base } OQ)\\]\" width=\"315\" height=\"18\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/9/e39f0bd6389dc4674b517afc33c9eb48bbb84754.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OFQ = \\angle OEQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/899899a2f10f1ac00c700d284d6530bd71dbac89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EOF$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is an isosceles triangle.\n</p>\n<ol><li><b>Conclusion:</b> In isosceles triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/899899a2f10f1ac00c700d284d6530bd71dbac89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EOF$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, the altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e523074f8e48f3c3e9e81ea84cfb36ddaa7b28a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> to base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39c134d9eeaf3bf929d13b7bdd2545673458401e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QE = QF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />.</li></ol>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Conclusion\">Conclusion</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Conclusion\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Combining Part 1 and Part 2, we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92ea2a95ac681a7b3c2307f16a0128ac44ea69b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QE = QF \\iff OQ \\perp EF. \\quad \\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"252\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/419473185b86cc35983f5a7baeaa93ee65e7bd8c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(250); import olympiad; defaultpen(linewidth(0.7) + fontsize(11pt));  // Given Angles real angB = 65; real angMOQ = 34;  // Coordinate Setup pair M = (0,0); pair B = (-5,0); pair C = (5,0);  // Calculate A so that angle B and angle C are 65 degrees pair A = (0, 5 * tan(angB * pi/180));  // Calculate O on AM such that OB is perpendicular to AB pair O = (0, -5 / tan(angB * pi/180));  // Calculate Q on BC right of M such that angle MOQ = 34 degrees pair Q = ( -O.y * tan(angMOQ * pi/180), 0);  // E and F lie on AB and AC, with EF passing through Q and perpendicular to OQ pair dirEF = rotate(90) * (Q - O); pair E = extension(A, B, Q, Q + dirEF); pair F = extension(A, C, Q, Q + dirEF);  // Draw the main triangle and extend AC to F draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(C--F); draw(A--O, dashed); draw(B--O--C);  draw(E--F); draw(O--Q); draw(E--O); draw(O--F);  // Helper function to mark right angles void mark_right_angle(pair p1, pair p2, pair p3, real s=0.3) {     pair d1 = unit(p1-p2) * s;     pair d2 = unit(p3-p2) * s;     draw(p2+d1 -- p2+d1+d2 -- p2+d2, gray); }  // Label the points dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SE); dot(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, NW); dot(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, S); dot(&quot;$Q$&quot;, Q, NE); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, W); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, S); [/asy]\" width=\"342\" height=\"418\" />\n</p><p>Clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/022a357881fa74c7f14bb5d78fb733d3378324a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MBO=\\angle MCO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"149\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/d/1bd2258be663d5ccb0a96e55683493159b7be3a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ\\perp EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/9/329e61e1e7742a3effd722c7c2dd88ab4273acec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EBO=\\angle EQO=\\angle FQO=\\angle FCO=90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"349\" height=\"18\" />. It follows that quadrilaterals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/5898b16b4e04e69e17d551fe1d07553f814c31c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEQO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/7/387cab14ec6a03ee1a43c529dcfb67c451f4ce97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CFOQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> are cyclic. Hence,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/b/a8b5ec9e8ad7d9b22db1abd283ad644c5a60fd26.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle MBO=\\angle QBO=\\angle QEO=\\angle MCO=\\angle QCO=\\angle QFO\\]\" width=\"466\" height=\"16\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/8/7e8ac37ddb8f498a6f63adbd8925f53ca35aa8e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EO=FO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />. Along with the perpendicularity condition and HL proves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/0/c506749d9f5435e20f4144fa3bc0a1c98f8a99ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EQO\\cong\\triangle FQO\\implies EQ=FQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"276\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/e/04e2191714383f3051e7ed122c42bb7ad8f303d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EQ=FQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />, by the Menelaus Theorem on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/8712c1ef923b8ffd7923e7e481ed3091b5944113.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be0ce0c38525d1160ddf70c1f628d7f616d2e0b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{AB}{BE}\\cdot\\frac{EQ}{FQ}\\cdot\\frac{CF}{AC}=1,\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"41\" />\nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/f/a7fc1ffea50d12630c3ba64326899a88cee44f2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=CF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />. Along with the conditions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b281e0fa1baadf171e7af6496bc3027a33796f89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MBO = \\angle MCO\\implies BO=CO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"280\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d4096420609d7c45a4b6d3801d90213d4f49cfaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EBO=\\angle FCO=90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"188\" height=\"15\" /> proves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9dd3eb08121c7cfdb905463c501fcd26e9d401f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EBO\\cong\\triangle FCO\\implies EO=FO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"276\" height=\"18\" />. By SSS, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/7/eb79dc1ebaf062fdeab3affe8f9539f22088749c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EQO\\cong\\triangle FQO\\implies \\angle EQO=\\angle FQO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"330\" height=\"18\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/e/c3e52027d435892a71dac6cc9cc459882a22c70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E,Q,F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> are collinear. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6be031a075f974e9f61f29b96b753cc2bbe134e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EQO=\\angle FQO=90^\\circ\\iff OQ\\perp EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"323\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15c9ff0788738359f3f2f9090041b7b7e225f3cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ\\perp EF \\iff EQ=FQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"219\" height=\"18\" />, as desired.\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO\" title=\"1994 IMO\">1994 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017004029\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.057 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.079 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 753/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 27367/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   10.642      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%   10.642      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21084:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017004029 and revision id 291679. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}